# This CITATION.cff lets GitHub show a "Cite this repository" button and
# seeds the Zenodo archive metadata. Update authors/version when they change,
# and add the Zenodo DOI after the first archive (see the bottom of this file).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RSAIRF, please cite it as below."
title: "Really Simple AI Risk Framework (RSAIRF)"
abstract: >-
  The Really Simple AI Risk Framework (RSAIRF) is a lightweight, practical
  framework for identifying, scoring, and tracking the risks that arise when
  organizations build, deploy, or use AI. At its core is a curated register of
  30 AI-specific risks, each mapped to the lifecycle stage where it typically
  appears and described in plain language. A simple likelihood x impact scoring
  model lets teams prioritize consistently without heavy tooling, and a
  ready-to-use risk log template turns the register into an auditable record of
  owners, controls, and review dates. Each risk is also cross-referenced to
  established AI governance and security standards, so findings connect directly
  to existing compliance and assurance work. RSAIRF is designed to be adopted in
  an afternoon and maintained as a living resource that teams can extend as new
  risks emerge.
# CFF only supports "software" or "dataset"; "dataset" is the closest fit for
# this risk register. The Zenodo record is classified as a report via .zenodo.json.
type: dataset
